WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.520
Delhi, or your state capital:

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.460
who writes the law?

3
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.630
Three lists settle it.

4
00:00:06.994 --> 00:00:08.194
The Seventh Schedule has three

5
00:00:08.194 --> 00:00:11.854
lists. Article 246 says who may

6
00:00:11.854 --> 00:00:13.364
legislate on each.

7
00:00:13.855 --> 00:00:14.875
The Union List:

8
00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:15.955
Parliament only.

9
00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:18.195
Defence, foreign affairs,

10
00:00:18.195 --> 00:00:20.435
railways, currency, banking.

11
00:00:20.435 --> 00:00:22.375
A Union currency spares us a

12
00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:24.185
different rupee in every state.

13
00:00:24.676 --> 00:00:25.576
The State List:

14
00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:27.096
the states only.

15
00:00:27.096 --> 00:00:29.216
Public order, police, public

16
00:00:29.216 --> 00:00:31.566
health, agriculture, land.

17
00:00:32.106 --> 00:00:33.126
The Concurrent List:

18
00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:35.846
both. Criminal law, marriage and

19
00:00:35.846 --> 00:00:38.466
divorce, education, forests,

20
00:00:38.466 --> 00:00:39.336
electricity.

21
00:00:40.094 --> 00:00:40.894
A clash?

22
00:00:41.514 --> 00:00:43.394
On a Concurrent subject,

23
00:00:43.394 --> 00:00:45.174
Parliament's law prevails.

24
00:00:45.174 --> 00:00:46.514
The exception:

25
00:00:46.514 --> 00:00:48.394
a state law the President has

26
00:00:48.394 --> 00:00:50.354
assented to holds in that state,

27
00:00:50.354 --> 00:00:52.114
though Parliament may legislate

28
00:00:52.114 --> 00:00:53.164
over it later.

29
00:00:53.743 --> 00:00:55.063
On no list at all?

30
00:00:55.063 --> 00:00:56.703
That is residuary:

31
00:00:56.703 --> 00:00:58.083
Parliament alone.

32
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.073
A rather tidy arrangement.

33
00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:01.938
For GS2:

34
00:01:01.938 --> 00:01:03.808
three lists, Article 246.

35
00:01:03.808 --> 00:01:07.908
On a clash, Parliament's law,

36
00:01:07.908 --> 00:01:08.808
Article 254.

37
00:01:08.808 --> 00:01:12.608
Residuary, Parliament, Article

38
00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:13.408
248.

39
00:01:15.195 --> 00:01:17.555
Union, State, or both.

40
00:01:17.555 --> 00:01:19.695
On a clash, Parliament usually

41
00:01:19.695 --> 00:01:21.245
has the last word.
